---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navigation from '../components/Navigation.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import Card from '../components/ui/Card.astro';
import Icon from '../components/ui/Icon.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Text Count Tools - Free Online Word Counter & Reading Time Calculator" 
  description="Free online word counter and reading time calculator. Count words, characters, sentences, paragraphs instantly. Upload PDF, DOCX, TXT files. 100% private, works offline, no limits."
  canonicalURL="https://textcounttools.com"
  ogImage="https://textcounttools.com/og-image.png"
  ogType="website"
>
  <Navigation />

  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="relative section-padding-lg mesh-gradient" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <div class="container-main">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto text-center">
          <p class="text-mono-eyebrow text-text-muted mb-6" style="letter-spacing: 0.1em;">Text Analysis Tools</p>
          <h1 id="hero-heading" class="text-display-xl text-text-primary mb-6 leading-tight">
            Fast, private text analysis<br class="hidden sm:block" />that runs in your browser
          </h1>
          <p class="text-body-lg text-text-secondary mb-10 prose-full text-center">
            Count words, calculate reading time, and analyze text instantly. No uploads, no tracking, no limits. Your data never leaves your device.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
            <a href="/tools/word-counter/" class="btn-primary text-button-lg h-12 px-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2" role="button">
              <Icon name="word" width="20" height="20" />
              Try Word Counter
            </a>
            <a href="/tools/reading-time-calculator/" class="btn-secondary text-button-lg h-12 px-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2" role="button">
              <Icon name="clock" width="20" height="20" />
              Calculate Reading Time
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SEO Content Section - 600+ words -->
    <section class="section-padding-lg" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <div class="container-main">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <h2 id="about-heading" class="text-heading-lg text-text-primary mb-8 text-center">Free Online Text Analysis Tools for Writers, Students & Professionals</h2>
          
          <div class="prose-full space-y-6 text-text-secondary">
            <p>
              <strong>Text Count Tools</strong> provides two essential text analysis utilities that run entirely in your browser: a <strong>Word Counter</strong> and a <strong>Reading Time Calculator</strong>. Unlike other online tools that send your content to external servers for processing, our text analyzer performs all calculations locally using JavaScript. This means your documents, essays, articles, and sensitive text never leave your device—guaranteeing complete privacy and data security.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-heading-md text-text-primary">Why Choose Our Word Counter Online?</h3>
            <p>
              Our <strong>free word counter</strong> goes beyond basic word counting. It delivers comprehensive text statistics in real-time as you type or paste content. The tool counts words, characters (with and without spaces), sentences, paragraphs, and lines. It also calculates average word length and average sentence length—metrics that help writers assess readability and flow. Whether you're a student checking an <strong>essay word counter</strong> for assignment requirements, a content creator optimizing for SEO character limits, or a professional preparing reports, our tool provides the precise data you need instantly.
            </p>
            <p>
              The word counter supports multiple input methods: type directly, paste text from clipboard, or upload files. We support <strong>TXT, Markdown (MD), PDF, and DOCX</strong> formats up to 10MB. Drag and drop files directly into the editor or click to browse. For PDF and DOCX files, the tool extracts text content automatically using client-side libraries (pdfjs-dist for PDFs, mammoth.js for Word documents), so you never need to copy-paste manually.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-heading-md text-text-primary">Reading Time Calculator for Better Content Planning</h3>
            <p>
              The <strong>Reading Time Calculator</strong> estimates how long it takes to read or speak any text. Choose from seven reading speed presets: Very Slow (100 WPM) for complex technical content, Academic Paper (150 WPM) for dense research, Scientific Journal (180 WPM), General Reading (200 WPM) for average adults, Novel/Fiction (250 WPM) for enjoyable reading, Fast Reader (300 WPM) for experienced speed readers, or set a <strong>custom words-per-minute</strong> value between 50-1000 WPM. The calculator also estimates <strong>speaking time</strong> at 130 WPM (average speaking pace) and shows an estimated finish time if you start reading now.
            </p>
            <p>
              This tool is invaluable for <strong>bloggers, podcasters, speech writers, educators, and students</strong>. Content creators can plan article length for target reading times. Speakers can estimate presentation duration. Students can gauge study time for assigned readings. The calculator works with the same file upload capabilities as the word counter, making it easy to analyze PDFs, Word docs, and text files without manual copying.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-heading-md text-text-primary">Privacy-First Architecture</h3>
            <p>
              Privacy is not an afterthought—it's the foundation of Text Count Tools. All text processing happens in your browser using WebAssembly and JavaScript. No data is transmitted to our servers, stored in databases, or logged. We don't use analytics, tracking pixels, or third-party scripts that could compromise your content. The tools work completely offline after the initial page load, thanks to Service Worker caching and Progressive Web App support. This makes Text Count Tools suitable for sensitive environments: legal documents, medical notes, confidential business reports, personal journals, and academic research.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-heading-md text-text-primary">Built for Modern Workflows</h3>
            <p>
              Both tools include productivity features: <strong>auto-save to localStorage</strong> preserves your text across browser sessions, <strong>copy statistics</strong> to clipboard in JSON format, <strong>download stats</strong> as a file, and <strong>clear text</strong> with one click. The <strong>dark/light mode</strong> adapts to system preference or manual toggle. The interface is fully responsive, accessible (WCAG 2.1 AA compliant), and works on mobile, tablet, and desktop. No registration, no subscriptions, no usage limits—just open the page and start analyzing text.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-heading-md text-text-primary">Who Uses Text Count Tools?</h3>
            <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2">
              <li><strong>Students & Academics:</strong> Essay word counter for assignments, thesis word limits, reading time estimation for research papers</li>
              <li><strong>Content Writers & Bloggers:</strong> SEO character limits, reading time for articles, content planning</li>
              <li><strong>Professionals:</strong> Report length checks, presentation timing, email brevity</li>
              <li><strong>Authors & Editors:</strong> Chapter word counts, manuscript pacing, reading time estimates</li>
              <li><strong>Developers:</strong> Documentation length, README word counts, commit message limits</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding" aria-labelledby="features-heading">
      <div class="container-main">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-16">
          <p class="text-mono-eyebrow text-text-muted mb-3">Tools</p>
          <h2 id="features-heading" class="text-heading-lg text-text-primary mb-4">Two powerful tools, zero compromises</h2>
          <p class="text-body-lg text-text-secondary prose-full">
            Each tool is built for a specific purpose with meticulous attention to detail.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <article class="card-feature-elevated p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800 flex items-center justify-center">
                <Icon name="word" width="24" height="24" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white" />
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-heading-md text-text-primary">Word Counter</h3>
                <p class="text-body-sm text-text-muted">Flagship tool</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-body-md text-text-secondary mb-6">
              Paste text, type directly, or upload files. Get instant statistics including words, characters, sentences, paragraphs, and averages.
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3 mb-6" role="list">
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Live word, character, sentence, paragraph counts
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Average word & sentence length
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                TXT, MD, PDF, DOCX file upload
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Drag & drop support
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Auto-save to localStorage
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Copy & download statistics
              </li>
            </ul>
            <a href="/tools/word-counter/" class="btn-primary text-button-lg h-12 px-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 w-full" role="button">
              Open Word Counter
              <Icon name="arrowRight" width="16" height="16" />
            </a>
          </article>

          <article class="card-feature-elevated p-8">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
              <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-lg bg-gray-100 dark:bg-gray-800 flex items-center justify-center">
                <Icon name="clock" width="24" height="24" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white" />
              </div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-heading-md text-text-primary">Reading Time Calculator</h3>
                <p class="text-body-sm text-text-muted">Time estimator</p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="text-body-md text-text-secondary mb-6">
              Calculate how long it takes to read or speak any text. Choose from presets or set your own reading speed.
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-3 mb-6" role="list">
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Multiple reading speed presets
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Custom words-per-minute input
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Estimated speaking time
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Estimated finish time
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                TXT, MD, PDF, DOCX file upload
              </li>
              <li class="flex items-center gap-3 text-body-md text-text-secondary">
                <Icon name="checkCircle" width="20" height="20" class="text-gray-900 dark:text-white flex-shrink-0" />
                Instant calculations
              </li>
            </ul>
            <a href="/tools/reading-time-calculator/" class="btn-primary text-button-lg h-12 px-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 w-full" role="button">
              Calculate Reading Time
              <Icon name="arrowRight" width="16" height="16" />
            </a>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

<section id="faq" class="section-padding" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
      <div class="container-main">
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto text-center mb-12">
          <p class="text-mono-eyebrow text-text-muted mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</p>
          <h2 id="faq-heading" class="text-heading-lg text-text-primary mb-4">Common questions</h2>
        </div>

        <dl class="space-y-4 max-w-4xl mx-auto">
          <!-- Word Counter Questions -->
          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  What statistics does the Word Counter show?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  The Word Counter displays: word count, character count (with and without spaces), sentence count, paragraph count, line count, average word length, and average sentence length. All statistics update in real-time as you type or paste text.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  Can I upload PDF and Word documents to the Word Counter?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  Yes. The Word Counter supports TXT, Markdown (MD), PDF, and DOCX files up to 10MB. Text is extracted client-side using pdfjs-dist for PDFs and mammoth.js for DOCX files—no server upload required.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  How do I copy or export word count statistics?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  Click the "Copy Stats" button to copy all statistics as formatted JSON to your clipboard, or use "Download Stats" to save a .json file with all metrics including timestamp.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  Does the Word Counter auto-save my text?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  Yes. Text is automatically saved to localStorage as you type. It persists across browser sessions and page refreshes. Use the "Clear" button to reset both the text and saved data.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <!-- Reading Time Calculator Questions -->
          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  Which reading speed preset should I choose?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  General Reading (200 WPM) works for most content. Use Academic Paper (150 WPM) for dense research, Scientific Journal (180 WPM) for technical papers, Novel/Fiction (250 WPM) for enjoyable reading, or set a custom WPM (50-1000) if you know your personal reading speed.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  What's the difference between reading time and speaking time?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  Reading time uses your selected WPM preset (default 200 WPM). Speaking time is fixed at 130 WPM—the average speaking pace for presentations and voiceovers. Speaking time is typically longer than silent reading time for the same text.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  Can the Reading Time Calculator handle PDF and DOCX files?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  Yes. Upload TXT, MD, PDF, or DOCX files (up to 10MB) and the calculator extracts text instantly to estimate reading and speaking time. No manual copy-pasting needed for documents.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  How is estimated finish time calculated?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  Finish time = current time + estimated reading duration. It shows when you'll finish if you start reading immediately. Useful for planning study sessions, presentations, or content consumption.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <!-- General Tool Questions -->
          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  Do these tools work without internet after loading?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  Yes. After the initial page load, both tools work completely offline. They're installed as a Progressive Web App with Service Worker caching—all text processing happens in your browser.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>

          <div class="card-feature">
            <dt>
              <details class="group">
                <summary class="flex items-center justify-between cursor-pointer list-none p-4 text-heading-md text-text-primary">
                  Is there a limit on text length or file size?
                  <Icon name="arrowRight" width="20" height="20" class="text-text-muted group-open:rotate-90 transition-transform" />
                </summary>
                <dd class="px-4 pb-4 text-body-md text-text-secondary prose-full">
                  No limit on pasted/typed text length. File uploads are limited to 10MB each (TXT, MD, PDF, DOCX). The tools efficiently handle very large texts without performance issues.
                </dd>
              </details>
            </dt>
          </div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding-lg mesh-gradient" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
      <div class="container-main">
        <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto text-center">
          <h2 id="cta-heading" class="text-display-xl text-text-primary mb-6 leading-tight">
            Ready to analyze your text?
          </h2>
          <p class="text-body-lg text-text-secondary mb-8 prose-full">
            Join thousands of writers, students, and professionals who trust Text Count Tools for fast, private text analysis.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-center gap-4">
            <a href="/tools/word-counter/" class="btn-primary text-button-lg h-12 px-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2" role="button">
              Start Counting Words
              <Icon name="arrowRight" width="16" height="16" />
            </a>
            <a href="/tools/reading-time-calculator/" class="btn-secondary text-button-lg h-12 px-6 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2" role="button">
              Calculate Reading Time
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Footer />
  </main>
</Layout>